WEBVTT

NOTE F9: single participant. Repeat with a known count (four sites, corrected to five at c16), a "for each extinguisher" repeat nested inside it (count varies), and an iteration (correct and resubmit until it passes validation) with typical passes and a limit of three rejections that triggers an error flow. Synthetic.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
<v Interviewer>Could you walk me through your monthly safety inspections?</v>

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:16.000
<v Sam Okafor>Sure. The goal is that every site is safe, and we've got the paperwork to prove it if the inspector turns up.</v>

3
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:22.000
<v Sam Okafor>I start by printing the inspection checklists, one per site.</v>

4
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:31.000
<v Sam Okafor>Then I go round each of our four sites, one after another, usually over two days.</v>

5
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:40.000
<v Sam Okafor>At each site I travel there, walk all the fire exits, then check the extinguishers.</v>

6
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:51.000
<v Sam Okafor>For each extinguisher I check the tag is in date. Depends on the site, the big warehouse has about thirty.</v>

7
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:59.000
<v Sam Okafor>I note any defects on the checklist, then sign the checklist off before I leave.</v>

8
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:03.000
<v Interviewer>How hard is the extinguisher check, one to five?</v>

9
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:07.000
<v Sam Okafor>A two. It's just tedious.</v>

10
00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:15.000
<v Sam Okafor>Back at the office I type up the report in the inspection portal and submit it.</v>

11
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:25.000
<v Sam Okafor>The portal validates it. If it fails, I correct it and submit again. Usually takes two goes.</v>

12
00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:32.000
<v Sam Okafor>If it gets rejected three times, I give up and ring the IT helpdesk.</v>

13
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:44.000
<v Sam Okafor>They fix whatever's wrong with the record and I submit it again. That's maybe every few months, and it's a nightmare.</v>

14
00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:50.000
<v Sam Okafor>Once it passes, I email a summary to the operations director.</v>

15
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:55.000
<v Sam Okafor>She reviews it, and that's the month done.</v>

16
00:01:55.000 --> 00:02:03.000
<v Sam Okafor>Oh, I said four sites. It's five now, we opened Leeds in the summer.</v>

17
00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:07.000
<v Interviewer>How long does it take altogether?</v>

18
00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:14.000
<v Sam Okafor>Two days on the road, and about half a day on the report.</v>
